WEBVTT

00:01:29.496 --> 00:01:31.371
not the ones that leaders impose.

00:01:31.413 --> 00:01:32.829
So talk to your team.

00:01:33.163 --> 00:01:36.829
My very favorite is the one
that you recommended, Trier:

00:01:36.829 --> 00:01:38.038
“purple flag.”

00:01:38.079 --> 00:01:40.538
When someone says
or does something biased,

00:01:40.579 --> 00:01:41.996
we'll say "purple flag."

00:01:42.038 --> 00:01:45.038
Maybe we'll even wave a purple flag.

00:01:45.038 --> 00:01:46.288
It's not a red flag.

00:01:46.329 --> 00:01:48.246
It's a friendly purple flag.

00:01:48.246 --> 00:01:50.788
TB: It helps us become more aware
of our blind spots.

00:01:51.288 --> 00:01:52.496
KS: Purple flag.

00:01:52.496 --> 00:01:53.663
TB: Purple flag.

00:01:53.704 --> 00:01:55.121
Thanks for pointing that out.

00:01:55.121 --> 00:01:57.746
I've been noticing lately
I use a lot of sight metaphors

00:01:57.788 --> 00:02:00.704
that often portray disabilities,
like being visually impaired,